{"name":"Only Yesterday","hex":"#f4d1b9","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"only","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alone in a category.","Singularly superior; the best."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Without others or anything further; exclusively.","No more than; just."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/only"},{"term":"yesterday","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The day immediately before today; one day ago.","The past, often in terms of being outdated."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["On the day before today.","As soon as possible."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/yesterday"}],"entries":[{"title":"Only Yesterday (1933 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Only Yesterday is a 1933 American pre-Code melodrama film, directed by John M. Stahl, about a young woman who becomes pregnant by her boyfriend before he rushes off to fight in World War I. It stars Margaret Sullavan and John Boles."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/4/48/Only-Yesterday-1933-Lobbycard.jpg/330px-Only-Yesterday-1933-Lobbycard.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Only_Yesterday_(1933_film)","wikidata":"Q1058231"},{"title":"Only Yesterday (1991 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Only Yesterday  is a 1991 Japanese animated drama film written and directed by Isao Takahata, based on the 1982 manga Omoide Poro Poro by Hotaru Okamoto and Yuko Tone. Produced by Toshio Suzuki, it was animated by Studio Ghibli for Tokuma Shoten, Nippon Television Network and Hakuhodo, and distributed by Toho. The film follows a twenty-seven-year-old Taeko Okajima as she takes a holiday with her relatives in the country; during the course of her trip, she reminisces about her life when she was ten. The ending theme song \"Ai wa Hana, Kimi wa sono Tane\"  is a Japanese translation of Amanda McBroom's composition \"The Rose\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/4/46/OYpost.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Only_Yesterday_(1991_film)","wikidata":"Q1045889"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Satoyama_Satellite_in_Kaisho_Forest_-_6.jpg/500px-Satoyama_Satellite_in_Kaisho_Forest_-_6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Satoyama_Satellite_in_Kaisho_Forest_-_6.jpg/1280px-Satoyama_Satellite_in_Kaisho_Forest_-_6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Satoyama_Satellite_in_Kaisho_Forest_-_6.jpg/500px-Satoyama_Satellite_in_Kaisho_Forest_-_6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Example picture of a satoyama, in Aichi Prefecture","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASatoyama_Satellite_in_Kaisho_Forest_-_6.jpg"}],"sounds":{"only":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/82/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-only.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/8/82/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-only.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-only.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/8/82/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-only.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-only.wav.ogg"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/ca/En-us-only.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/c/ca/En-us-only.ogg/En-us-only.ogg.mp3"},{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/comm